[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_s")
id = "quartermaster"
display_name = "The Quartermaster"
title = "The Quartermaster"
category = "Resources"
order = 31
image = "res://art/guide/quartermaster.png"
body = "Gold buys towers, and towers run out. Once every emplacement is filled and every level the Forge allows is bought, a purse that keeps growing is a purse that has stopped meaning anything.

The Quartermaster is where the rest of it goes. During Preparation you may place a standing order: mend the wall, mend the towers, or rearm every trap you have laid. The button offers whichever of the three would actually do something.

Every order costs more than the one before it, for the whole run, with no ceiling. That is the design rather than a limit: a sink you can empty stops being a sink, and a price that stops rising turns a big purse into a second economy.

Nothing the Quartermaster sells is new. Every order buys back something you already had and already paid for. Wood is still the cheap way to mend a wall and there is still only so much of it; Gold is the way there is always more of, and it gets dearer."
